 "name": "Italian motorway tolls (ESTIMATE: each concession's unit rate per km)",
 "law": "Estimate. Italian motorway tolls are each concession's unit rate per km, by vehicle class (A, B by height for two axles; 3, 4, 5 by axles) and by plain or mountain stretch, plus the ANAS surcharge (law 102/2009 art. 19 c. 9-bis), times the km between toll stations, plus 22% VAT, rounded to 10 cents (the concession agreements with the Ministry, under the State's laws and CIPE resolutions). No station-to-station table can be fetched, so the route's km on toll motorways (OpenStreetMap ways tagged toll=yes) are priced by the operator OpenStreetMap gives the ways: Superstrada Pedemontana Veneta and Autostrade per l'Italia's mountain stretches as its route calculator prices them (the A1 Bologna-Calenzano, A7 Serravalle-Genova, A10 Genova-Savona, A12 Genova-Sestri Levante, A16 Baiano-Candela, A23 Carnia-Tarvisio, A26 Genova Voltri-Alessandria Sud and Gravellona Toce-Lago Maggiore, A27 Conegliano-Belluno; their rates in Autostrade per l'Italia's toll calculator file, which gives Autostrade per l'Italia's own plain rates as its page does), Autostrada del Brennero (A22; Brennero-Affi at its mountain rate, placed by the Affi junction in OpenStreetMap), Asti-Cuneo (A33), Ivrea Torino Piacenza (A5, A55), Autostrada dei Fiori (A6; its 2025 unit rate raised by the change its notice states), Autovia Padana (A21 Piacenza-Brescia), Brebemi (A35), Brescia-Padova (A4 Brescia-Padova, A31), CAV (A4, A57, Passante di Mestre), Milano Serravalle (A7; its 2025 unit rate raised by the increase its page states), Pedemontana Lombarda (A36, A59, A60), RAV (A5 Aosta-Courmayeur), SALT (A15; its 2025 unit rate raised by the change its notice states), SAT (A12 Livorno-Civitavecchia), SATAP (A4 Torino-Milano), Ivrea Torino Piacenza (A21), SAV (A5 Quincinetto-Aosta), Tangenziale Esterna (A58; its 2025 unit rate raised by the change its notice states) at the 2026 rates their own pages give (with VAT and the ANAS fee); the Consorzio per le Autostrade Siciliane's A18 and A20 by entry and exit in their own table (it-cas), and the open systems of Milan's ring roads (A50, A51, A52), SITAF's A32 Torino-Bardonecchia, Autostrade per l'Italia's A8 Milano-Varese, A9 Lainate-Como and A12 Roma-Civitavecchia, Salerno Pompei Napoli's A3 and the Tangenziale di Torino (A55) at their barriers (it-barriers), not here; the other concessions with a published sheet at their unit rate for 2025, ANAS surcharge and VAT included, as their sheets sent to the Ministry of Infrastructure and Transport (Directive (EU) 2022/362 art. 11, published March 2025) state them (the year's change, 1.5% on most networks in 2026, isn't applied to them: the Ministry's note couldn't be found, and their own pages state neither the year's rates nor the change), each concession's plain-stretch rate unless it has only mountain stretches; Autostrade per l'Italia's network and the concessions without rates in their sheet at Autostrade per l'Italia's plain-stretch unit rate, VAT included, in force from 2026-01-01: class B 0.08054, 3 0.10615, 4 0.16108, 5 0.19034 euro per km. Pedemontana Lombarda's classes are its own (3 trucks up to three axles, 4 articulated or with trailer). Mountain stretches cost about 18% more on ASPI's network (class 5 0.22437), SATAP's A4 east of Novara Est (its tariff B) and CAV's Passante di Mestre and A57 are priced at their own rates (placed by the motorway junctions in OpenStreetMap); the other open-system stretches charge fixed tolls, and the rounding isn't modelled, so the true toll can differ.",
